bg3le Ext.UI: validate property values before boxing; enumerate a DependencyObject's values safely

On top of 0001-0005. claude-run-2 S017 ended at 32 min in a SIGSEGV
(bg3le-20261010-025152.log.528429): signal 11 at 0x100, pc
push_boxed_or_object+0x30, the first `obj->GetClassType()`, with
val = r12 = 0x100. Caller: l_properties+0x3b0, the DependencyObject branch
(the mValues loop; push_stored and push_value inlined/tail-called), from
GetAllProperties on the client tick. The game was in choose_dialogue
"Sever your connection with Ragzlin" (Dror Ragzlin / dead mind flayer); the
dialogue job re-reads the rendered answers each tick, and UI.inlineText
called GetAllProperties on every Run of every answer text while the answer
list was being re-templated. One of a Run's stored values held 0x100 where
its property's type said BaseObject: not an object pointer (a freed or
replaced StoredValue/ComplexValue block, or the values table changing under
the walk), boxed without a check.

- push_boxed_or_object checks the value with plausible_object (safe reads of
  its vtable and first slots, which must be code of the game or bg3le) and
  pushes nil otherwise; so does push_value for an ICommand (plausible_vtable)
  before its virtual GetBaseObject. Counted (UiSerialize's 8th result) and
  logged (the first 20, then at powers of two) with the property's name.
- push_stored copies the StoredValue entry and its ComplexValue block out with
  safe reads (into raw buffers: StoredValue's constructor is the game's, and a
  ComplexValue copy would release its Ptr<Expression>).
- UiProperties copies a DependencyObject's keys first and looks each up again
  (push_dependency) before reading it: pushing allocates, a collection can run
  __gc, and the hash table is never walked across that. The owner is held
  (arg 1 is a box with a reference).
- UiProperties enumerates those values only when the call holds the UI lock
  (serialized() records it; 0002 runs a call unserialized after a 50 ms wait):
  otherwise the caller gets the plain properties only.

The mod side stops calling GetAllProperties on live elements (Client/UI.lua:
UI.get / UI.pick read named properties; inlineText, press, pressButton use
them).

